# "Focus Timer" – A Minimalist Pomodoro App with Tkinter

This app is a professional, visually appealing Pomodoro-style focus timer. It helps users work in focused intervals (25 minutes by default) followed by short breaks, boosting productivity and time management.

---

**Features:**
- Clean, modern interface using professional colors and fonts
- Start/Stop/Reset controls
- Visual countdown display
- Session tracking (work/break)
- Responsive layout with frames for structure

---

### Code

```python
import tkinter as tk
from tkinter import font as tkfont

# --- Configuration ---
WORK_MIN = 25   # Work session length in minutes
BREAK_MIN = 5   # Break session length in minutes

PRIMARY_COLOR = "#2E4053"
ACCENT_COLOR = "#58D68D"
BG_COLOR = "#F4F6F7"
FONT_MAIN = ("Segoe UI", 24, "bold")
FONT_SUBTITLE = ("Segoe UI", 14)
FONT_TIMER = ("Consolas", 48)

class FocusTimerApp(tk.Tk):
    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__()
        self.title("Focus Timer")
        self.geometry("380x300")
        self.configure(bg=BG_COLOR)
        self.resizable(False, False)

        # State variables
        self.is_running = False
        self.is_work_session = True
        self.time_left_sec = WORK_MIN * 60
        
        # Fonts (for scaling on different systems)
        tkfont.nametofont("TkDefaultFont").configure(size=12)

        # Layout frames for structure and color separation 
        header_frame = tk.Frame(self, bg=PRIMARY_COLOR)
        header_frame.pack(fill="x")

        content_frame = tk.Frame(self, bg=BG_COLOR)
        content_frame.pack(expand=True, fill="both")

        controls_frame = tk.Frame(self, bg=BG_COLOR)
        controls_frame.pack(pady=(0,15))
```

